<visual_directives>
5. VISUAL DESIGN DIRECTIVES
5.1 Typography System
Type Scale
Use a constrained, intentional scale — not arbitrary sizes:
```
Display:   text-5xl → text-7xl, tracking-tighter, leading-none, font-bold/black
Headline:  text-3xl → text-4xl, tracking-tight, leading-tight, font-semibold
Title:     text-xl → text-2xl, tracking-tight, leading-snug, font-medium
Body:      text-base → text-lg, leading-relaxed, max-w-\\\[65ch]
Label:     text-sm, tracking-wide, uppercase, font-medium (for form labels, table headers)
Caption:   text-xs, leading-normal (for timestamps, metadata)
Mono:      font-mono for all numbers in data-dense UIs, code, and technical values
```
Font Selection Rules
Default stack: `Geist`, `Satoshi`, `Cabinet Grotesk`, or `Outfit`
Inter is banned. Roboto, Arial, and system-ui defaults are banned.
Serif fonts are banned in dashboards, SaaS UIs, and data-dense applications. Allowed only in editorial, magazine, or creative contexts.
Pair a distinctive display/heading font with a refined body font. Never use two decorative fonts in the same project.
Load fonts from Google Fonts or Bunny Fonts via `@import` in CSS or `<link>` in head
Hierarchy via Weight + Color, Not Size
Avoid an H1 that "screams." Control prominence using `font-weight` and color contrast, not just `font-size`
Body text: `text-slate-600` (light mode) / `text-slate-400` (dark mode)
Secondary/metadata text: `text-slate-400` / `text-slate-500`
Interactive text links: accent color, underline on hover, never underlined by default in UI contexts (only in long-form prose)
5.2 Color System
Palette Architecture
```
Background:    1 color  (off-white, zinc-950, slate-900 — never pure #000 or #fff)
Surface:       1–2 colors (card, panel, elevated)
Border:        1 color (low-contrast, 1px dividers)
Text Primary:  1 color
Text Secondary: 1 color (subdued)
Accent:        1 color maximum (brand color, interactive states)
Semantic:      3 fixed colors (red/error, green/success, amber/warning)
```
Color Rules
Maximum 1 accent color per project; saturation < 80%
AI Purple Ban: No purple button glows, no neon blue-purple gradients. These signal "default AI output"
No pure black (#000000): use Zinc-950, Slate-950, or a very dark warm off-black (#0a0a0a)
No pure white (#ffffff) for large backgrounds: use #f9fafb, #fafaf9, or slate-50
Warm and cool grays must not be mixed in the same project — pick one temperature and commit
Accent color must pass contrast requirements when used on both light and dark backgrounds
Use CSS variables for all color tokens: `--color-accent`, `--color-surface`, not hardcoded Tailwind values
Semantic Color Discipline
Red: errors only (not for warnings, not for "important notices")
Green: success, completion, positive delta
Amber/Orange: warnings, pending states, caution
Blue (when not the accent): informational notices, links in prose
Dark Mode
Implement dark mode with `prefers-color-scheme` media query + a manual toggle (store preference in `localStorage`)
Never use `dark:` Tailwind classes without also defining the light variant
Dark mode surfaces must be layered, not flat: `bg-zinc-950` → `bg-zinc-900` → `bg-zinc-800` for depth
5.3 Layout & Spatial Composition
Grid Principles (by DESIGN_VARIANCE)
```
1–3 (Symmetric):   12-column grid, equal gutters, center-aligned sections, predictable rhythm
4–7 (Offset):       Asymmetric split (60/40, 70/30), overlapping elements, varied vertical rhythm
8–10 (Asymmetric): Masonry, fractional grid units (2fr 1fr 1fr), intentional void space, 20vw+ margins
```
Anti-Pattern: Center-Bias Override
When `DESIGN\\\_VARIANCE > 4`, centered hero sections are banned. Use:
Split-screen (left content / right asset)
Left-aligned text with right-aligned negative space
Diagonal text flow breaking the grid
Spacing System
Use a strict 4px base unit: all spacing values are multiples of 4 (`4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 80, 96…`).
Never use arbitrary pixel values like `13px`, `22px`, `37px` — they signal unintentional design.
Card Usage Policy
Cards communicate elevation and containment. Use them only when grouping content that is interactive as a unit, or when one group must stand out against its background.
Cards are banned for purely visual decoration in data-dense UIs (`VISUAL\\\_DENSITY > 7`). Use `border-t`, `divide-y`, or whitespace to create grouping without boxing.
When a shadow is used on a card, tint it to the surface background color (not neutral black). Example: a warm background gets `box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(120, 80, 40, 0.08)`.
All major card containers: `rounded-2xl` (standard) or `rounded-\\\[2.5rem]` (premium/Bento-style)
Anti-Patterns to Eliminate
Three equal-width cards in a row for feature lists: use a 2-column zigzag, asymmetric Bento, or horizontal scroll instead
Full-width hero image with centered text overlay: use left/right split with gradient fade to background color
"Wall of text" sections: break with a pull-quote, inline stat, or illustrative element every 3–4 paragraphs
5.4 Visual Effects & Materiality
Glassmorphism (Correct Implementation)
```css
/\\\* Basic glass — not enough \\\*/
backdrop-filter: blur(12px);

/\\\* Premium glass with edge refraction \\\*/
backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(1.8);
background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1), 0 16px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
```
Shadows
Tint shadows to the surface color, never use pure `rgba(0,0,0,X)` on colored backgrounds
Shadow layering: `shadow-sm` for subtle lift, `shadow-md` for cards, `shadow-xl` for modals/popovers
Avoid shadow spam: choose one elevation level per UI layer, not ad-hoc per component
Elevated interactive elements (buttons, cards) must increase shadow on hover for lift feedback
Backgrounds & Atmosphere
Prefer atmospheric backgrounds over flat solid colors for hero/feature sections:
Mesh gradients (CSS radial blobs via `@property` or SVG filters)
Subtle noise/grain textures applied to a `fixed` pseudo-element (never on a scrolling container — GPU repaint cost)
Geometric grid patterns with low opacity
Never use Unsplash URLs — use `https://picsum.photos/seed/{unique-string}/1200/800` or SVG-based placeholders
Stock photo placeholders must use unique seed strings per image, never the same seed twice
</visual_directives>
