9. FORBIDDEN PATTERNS (ANTI-SLOP REFERENCE)
The following patterns indicate generic AI output. Actively avoid every item on this list.
Visual
Neon outer glows on buttons or cards
Pure black (#000) or pure white (#fff) backgrounds
Purple/blue gradient overlays on dark hero sections
Oversaturated accent colors (saturation > 80%)
Gradient text on large headings as a default aesthetic
Generic `box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` repeated identically on every card
Decorative custom cursors
Typography
Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system-ui as the chosen typeface
Serif fonts on dashboards or data UIs
Overscaled H1 that dominates the page without proportional visual hierarchy
Layout
Three equal-width cards in a horizontal row for feature sections
Centered hero section (when DESIGN_VARIANCE > 4)
Asymmetric desktop layouts that overflow horizontally on mobile
`h-screen` for full-height sections
Content
"John Doe" / "Jane Smith" / "User 1" names
Generic SVG avatar silhouettes
Round numbers: 50%, 100%, $1,000
"Acme", "Nexus", "SmartFlow", "TechCorp" brand names
Filler CTA copy: "Get started", "Learn more", "Elevate your workflow"
Code
`window.addEventListener('scroll')` for animation triggers
`useState` for continuous animation values
Mixing Framer Motion + GSAP in the same component
Perpetual animations not isolated in `React.memo`
Missing loading, empty, or error states
`z-index: 9999` or arbitrary z-index stacking
Emojis in any context
</anti_patterns>
10. PRE-FLIGHT CHECKLIST
Evaluate every generated output against this matrix before finalizing:
UX Completeness
[ ] All interactive elements have defined hover, active, focus, and disabled states
[ ] Forms have label-above-input, inline validation, and error messages
[ ] All lists/tables/grids have designed empty states
